commit d9da2710abcfdc76a8456288894e66f1597034b7
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 17:43:28 2026 +0000

    Keep the bare link's look under the layer and return the 16 percentage names to Bootstrap (unit AS5)
    
    An $unscoped form, empty in the Bootstrap partials and naming the a tag
    in the layer's tokens, copies the reboot's link, hover, and undo rules at
    the reboot's specificity before the first component rule, so a bare link
    keeps its link color and underline under the layer while nav-link, btn,
    and no-underline keep theirs (the user's ruling R1 of 2026-10-07). The 16
    percentage names leave $withhold, so Bootstrap's important percentage
    rules apply under the layer by importance (ruling R3): w-100 reads 100%
    of its parent where Tailwind's rule read 400px; the carousel slides and
    the pinned badge return to Bootstrap's spelling, the Sizing section
    loses its clipping frames and multiples captions, the confinement case
    inverts, and the two negative controls that planted a percentage move to
    a different percentage. ./bootstrap stays byte-identical (332,388 bytes).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fwYCgxCd9JhL43kVBLBJV

